; Loading the same reader-macro definition twice is not a collision.
;
; A program can reach one `(reader-macros/define ...)` form twice -- most
; often a `#use-reader-macros` of a module's file followed by an import of
; that module, which registers the module's defines again.  Re-registering an
; identical definition (same delimiter, mode and template) is a no-op; only a
; DIFFERENT definition under the same name is the "already registered" error
; (errors/reader-macros-strict-collision).

#use-reader-macros "macros.tur"
#use-reader-macros "macros.tur"

(println #twice[20 22])   ; 42
